# sweep-keep — agents `parlay sweep` must never tear down.
#
# One agent id per line. Blank lines and `#` comments are ignored.
# Read by `parlay sweep` (tools/cli/internal/commands/sweep.go) from
# $PARLAY_STATE_HOME/sweep-keep (default ~/.parlay/sweep-keep).
#
# CHANGE THIS: list your own long-lived agents. Anything not listed here is
# eligible for teardown once `parlay crew-state` reports it finished. Short-lived
# task agents belong nowhere in this file — being swept is what you want for them.
#
# The file is optional. With no sweep-keep at all, only the sweeping agent itself
# and agents held for a human decision (needs-decision / blocked / failed) are
# protected.

# The long-lived general-purpose agent from this example. It is never "done", so
# without this line a sweep could still collect it after a terminal status line.
helm
